1b:["$","section",null,{"className":"related-section","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"site-shell","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":["$","h2",null,{"children":"Continue with a relevant guide"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"related-grid","children":[["$","$L5","guides/mext-application-routes",{"href":"/guides/mext-application-routes/","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Japan government scholarship guide"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"MEXT scholarship: embassy vs university recommendation"}],["$","$L6",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$7:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","$L5","guides/weighted-vs-unweighted-gpa",{"href":"/guides/weighted-vs-unweighted-gpa/","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"US student planning"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Weighted vs unweighted GPA: compare the same academic record"}],["$","$L6",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$7:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","$L5","tools/gpa-calculator-with-retakes",{"href":"/tools/gpa-calculator-with-retakes/","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"US student planning"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"GPA calculator with retakes: compare repeat policies"}],["$","$L6",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$7:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","$L5","tools",{"href":"/tools/","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Free planning tools · no account required"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Free student calculators and planning tools"}],["$","$L6",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$7:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}]]}]]}]}]
1d:["$","section","0-Choose a documented mapping before entering course records",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-1","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Choose a documented mapping before entering course records"}],[["$","p","The linked NIG appendix shows a three-point MEXT mapping. Its four-category A/B/C/F row maps to 3/2/1/0; the five-category S/A/B/C/F row maps to 3/3/2/1/0. These labels describe that appendix, not every transcript using letters.",{"children":"The linked NIG appendix shows a three-point MEXT mapping. Its four-category A/B/C/F row maps to 3/2/1/0; the five-category S/A/B/C/F row maps to 3/3/2/1/0. These labels describe that appendix, not every transcript using letters."}],["$","p","Confirm the applicable rule with the actual receiving host. If your transcript uses plus/minus marks or percentages that do not match the supported table, do not silently place them in the nearest category. Keep the original mark and request the host’s interpretation. A calculator should leave an unsupported scale unresolved rather than produce a confident-looking estimate.",{"children":"Confirm the applicable rule with the actual receiving host. If your transcript uses plus/minus marks or percentages that do not match the supported table, do not silently place them in the nearest category. Keep the original mark and request the host’s interpretation. A calculator should leave an unsupported scale unresolved rather than produce a confident-looking estimate."}]],"$undefined",[["$","p",null,{"className":"table-scroll-hint","children":"On a small screen, scroll the table sideways to compare all columns."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-table-wrap","role":"region","aria-label":"Named NIG appendix mapping","tabIndex":0,"children":["$","table",null,{"className":"guide-table","children":[["$","caption",null,{"children":"Named NIG appendix mapping"}],["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[[["$","th","Source category",{"scope":"col","children":"Source category"}],["$","th","Three-point value",{"scope":"col","children":"Three-point value"}],["$","th","Important boundary",{"scope":"col","children":"Important boundary"}]],"$undefined"]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Four-category A/B/C/F"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"3/2/1/0"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Use only when this row actually applies"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Five-category S/A/B/C/F"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"3/3/2/1/0"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"S and A share 3 points in this row"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Unsupported mark"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"No automatic value"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Obtain a host instruction"}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}]}],"$undefined"],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
1e:["$","section","1-Compute the weighted result from included courses",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-2","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Compute the weighted result from included courses"}],[["$","p","The credit-weighted formula is the sum of mapped points multiplied by credits, divided by the sum of included credits. The appendix gives a course-count method where the institution has no credit system, and excludes unlisted results such as Pass or Approved. This does not authorise dropping a supported failing grade.",{"children":"The credit-weighted formula is the sum of mapped points multiplied by credits, divided by the sum of included credits. The appendix gives a course-count method where the institution has no credit system, and excludes unlisted results such as Pass or Approved. This does not authorise dropping a supported failing grade."}],["$","p","Keep a record of the course, original grade, mapped value and credit weight. Review the record against the transcript before calculating. An empty credit field should remain an input error, rather than becoming zero and hiding a course. A genuine no-credit-system case needs its own clearly labelled mode; it is not the same as forgetting to enter the credits.",{"children":"Keep a record of the course, original grade, mapped value and credit weight. Review the record against the transcript before calculating. An empty credit field should remain an input error, rather than becoming zero and hiding a course. A genuine no-credit-system case needs its own clearly labelled mode; it is not the same as forgetting to enter the credits."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
1f:["$","section","2-Worked example: keep 8/3 visible before host rounding",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Worked example: keep 8/3 visible before host rounding"}],[["$","p","Consider a fictional record with two included credits mapped to 3 and one included credit mapped to 2. The numerator is 2×3+1×2=8 and the denominator is 3. The exact result is 8/3, approximately 2.6666667. Keeping those intermediate totals visible makes an incorrect weighting easier to detect.",{"children":"Consider a fictional record with two included credits mapped to 3 and one included credit mapped to 2. The numerator is 2×3+1×2=8 and the denominator is 3. The exact result is 8/3, approximately 2.6666667. Keeping those intermediate totals visible makes an incorrect weighting easier to detect."}],["$","p","Now compare the simple mean of the two mapped values: (3+2)/2=2.5. That would ignore the different credit weights. It is appropriate only for a genuinely equal-weight course-count calculation under the applicable rule. Do not switch methods because one gives a more favourable result.",{"children":"Now compare the simple mean of the two mapped values: (3+2)/2=2.5. That would ignore the different credit weights. It is appropriate only for a genuinely equal-weight course-count calculation under the applicable rule. Do not switch methods because one gives a more favourable result."}]],"$undefined",[["$","p",null,{"className":"table-scroll-hint","children":"On a small screen, scroll the table sideways to compare all columns."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-table-wrap","role":"region","aria-label":"Original unequal-credit calculation audit","tabIndex":0,"children":["$","table",null,{"className":"guide-table","children":[["$","caption",null,{"children":"Original unequal-credit calculation audit"}],["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[[["$","th","Course",{"scope":"col","children":"Course"}],["$","th","Mapped points",{"scope":"col","children":"Mapped points"}],["$","th","Credits",{"scope":"col","children":"Credits"}],["$","th","Quality points",{"scope":"col","children":"Quality points"}]],"$undefined"]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Fictional course A"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"3"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"2"}],["$","td","3",{"children":"6"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Fictional course B"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"2"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"1"}],["$","td","3",{"children":"2"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Included total"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"—"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"3"}],["$","td","3",{"children":"8"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","3",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Raw ratio"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"8÷3"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"—"}],["$","td","3",{"children":"2.6666667…"}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}]}],"$undefined"],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
20:["$","section","3-Exclusions should be visible in a separate record",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Exclusions should be visible in a separate record"}],[["$","p","Create an exclusions note beside the included-course table. State the original result, why it is excluded and the host instruction supporting that treatment. This prevents an omitted pass-only course from being mistaken for a forgotten row and makes the denominator easier to reconstruct.",{"children":"Create an exclusions note beside the included-course table. State the original result, why it is excluded and the host instruction supporting that treatment. This prevents an omitted pass-only course from being mistaken for a forgotten row and makes the denominator easier to reconstruct."}],["$","p","For a fictional transcript containing a Pass seminar and a graded failed course, the Pass result may be outside the specified calculation while the supported failing grade remains in the record. Do not re-label either result to improve the total. If a repeated course or a changed curriculum creates uncertainty, ask which attempts the receiving scheme wants rather than borrowing a generic GPA replacement policy.",{"children":"For a fictional transcript containing a Pass seminar and a graded failed course, the Pass result may be outside the specified calculation while the supported failing grade remains in the record. Do not re-label either result to improve the total. If a repeated course or a changed curriculum creates uncertainty, ask which attempts the receiving scheme wants rather than borrowing a generic GPA replacement policy."}]],"$undefined",[["$","p",null,{"className":"table-scroll-hint","children":"On a small screen, scroll the table sideways to compare all columns."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-table-wrap","role":"region","aria-label":"Original exclusion and uncertainty log","tabIndex":0,"children":["$","table",null,{"className":"guide-table","children":[["$","caption",null,{"children":"Original exclusion and uncertainty log"}],["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[[["$","th","Record",{"scope":"col","children":"Record"}],["$","th","Question",{"scope":"col","children":"Question"}],["$","th","Treatment",{"scope":"col","children":"Treatment"}]],"$undefined"]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Pass-only result"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"Does the named rule exclude it?"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Keep an exclusion note"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Supported F grade"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"Is it a regular included course?"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Do not silently remove it"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Retake or transfer course"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"Which host rule applies?"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Obtain clarification before reporting"}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}]}],"$undefined"],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
21:["$","section","4-A numeric result does not decide the application",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-5","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"A numeric result does not decide the application"}],[["$","p","The named appendix uses a 2.3 minimum and also sets a route-specific alternative when the table cannot be applied. Those details belong to that document and its host context. They should not become an automatic eligible/ineligible badge for every MEXT route.",{"children":"The named appendix uses a 2.3 minimum and also sets a route-specific alternative when the table cannot be applied. Those details belong to that document and its host context. They should not become an automatic eligible/ineligible badge for every MEXT route."}],["$","p","Even an accurately calculated estimate cannot establish nationality, degree completion, field fit, nomination availability or other conditions. Keep a separate eligibility checklist from the owner. The purpose of the tool is to make one calculation transparent while leaving the actual application decision with the institution and scheme.",{"children":"Even an accurately calculated estimate cannot establish nationality, degree completion, field fit, nomination availability or other conditions. Keep a separate eligibility checklist from the owner. The purpose of the tool is to make one calculation transparent while leaving the actual application decision with the institution and scheme."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
22:["$","section","5-Handle precision and reporting as a separate host instruction",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Handle precision and reporting as a separate host instruction"}],[["$","p","The appendix says to omit a fractional number but does not identify the precision clearly in the extracted wording. The tool should therefore show the unrounded ratio and a labelled decimal approximation, with a prompt to check the host’s reporting rule. It should not guess that a particular number of decimal places controls selection.",{"children":"The appendix says to omit a fractional number but does not identify the precision clearly in the extracted wording. The tool should therefore show the unrounded ratio and a labelled decimal approximation, with a prompt to check the host’s reporting rule. It should not guess that a particular number of decimal places controls selection."}],["$","p","When submitting an actual application, record the host, route, document date, included credits and the rounding instruction you used. Keep the calculator output as a working check alongside the original transcript. If the portal asks for a different calculation, follow that instruction and do not paste a planning estimate into a field requesting an official transcript GPA.",{"children":"When submitting an actual application, record the host, route, document date, included credits and the rounding instruction you used. Keep the calculator output as a working check alongside the original transcript. If the portal asks for a different calculation, follow that instruction and do not paste a planning estimate into a field requesting an official transcript GPA."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","nav",null,{"className":"answer-links","aria-label":"Next steps for Handle precision and reporting as a separate host instruction","children":[["$","$L5","/guides/mext-application-routes/",{"href":"/guides/mext-application-routes/","children":["Understand MEXT application routes",["$","$L6",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$7:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","$L5","/guides/weighted-vs-unweighted-gpa/",{"href":"/guides/weighted-vs-unweighted-gpa/","children":["Check weighted GPA assumptions",["$","$L6",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$7:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","$L5","/tools/",{"href":"/tools/","children":["Compare other planning tools",["$","$L6",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$7:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}]]}]]}]
23:["$","section",null,{"className":"source-section","aria-labelledby":"official-sources","children":[["$","h2",null,{"id":"official-sources","children":"Official sources and verification"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Source records support the guide. Page update dates describe editorial changes; they do not mean every linked rule was checked again today. Reopen the current call for your programme and intake."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"source-grid","children":[["$","$L5","https://www.nig.ac.jp/wp/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/AboutMextGPA.pdf",{"href":"https://www.nig.ac.jp/wp/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/AboutMextGPA.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"National Institute of Genetics: MEXT GPA appendix PDF"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Both PDF pages and grade-table/formula screenshots reviewed 23 November 2026. Named appendix example, not universal equivalence. Fractional precision is not specified clearly; calculator must show raw result without guessing host rounding."}]]}],["$","$L6",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M15 3h6v6","key":"1q9fwt"}],["path",{"d":"M10 14 21 3","key":"gplh6r"}],["path",{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6","key":"a6xqqp"}]],"className":"lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}]]}]]}]
